  "recipe": {
    "technique": "Unlike many drawing media, where the artist adds in the mid-tones and shadows, with scratchboard the artist is working by adding in the highlights. The artist can use a variety of tools to scratch away the black ink from the board and reveal more or less of the white clay that is underneath. Effects include stippling by poking the board with a needle or blade, and scratching or cross-hatching using a sharp blade."
